msgid "September 2026 {#september-2026}"
msgstr "September 2026 {#september-2026}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "New tools have been built on top of the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) framework, which was released earlier this year:\n"
msgstr "Alat baharu telah dibina di atas rangka kerja [model pelaksanaan terarah](/guides/directed-execution-model), yang dikeluarkan awal tahun ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) is a toolkit for randomization-based quantum noise characterization. You can use it to construct a custom noise-learning experiment, validate it with local simulation, and analyze the raw results.\n"
msgstr "[`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) ialah kit alat untuk pencirian hingar kuantum berasaskan rawak. Anda boleh menggunakannya untuk membina eksperimen pembelajaran hingar tersuai, mengesahkannya dengan simulasi tempatan, dan menganalisis hasil mentah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) is a package of quantum error mitigation methods for building mitigation pipelines with the new execution model. It includes implementations of well-known methods, including PEC, PEA, TREX, and gate-folding ZNE, as well as post-selection for filtering out non-Markovian errors.\n"
msgstr "[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) ialah pakej kaedah mitigasi ralat kuantum untuk membina saluran paip mitigasi dengan model pelaksanaan baharu. Ia merangkumi pelaksanaan kaedah yang terkenal, termasuk PEC, PEA, TREX, dan ZNE gate-folding, serta post-selection untuk menapis ralat bukan-Markov.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "August 2026 {#august-2026}"
msgstr "Ogos 2026 {#august-2026}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) had its first release this month! This package provides tools for working with fermionic systems, including building fermionic operators and circuits, implementing fermion-to-qubit encodings, and circuit synthesis through the Qiskit transpiler integration. Qiskit Fermions can be used with other complementary tools in the ecosystem, such as `ffsim` (see this [documentation](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/ffsim) for more information) and the [SQD addon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), to build advanced workflows for fermionic systems. \n"
msgstr "[Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) mengeluarkan versi pertamanya bulan ini! Pakej ini menyediakan alat untuk bekerja dengan sistem fermion, termasuk membina operator dan litar fermion, melaksanakan pengekodan fermion-ke-qubit, dan sintesis litar melalui integrasi Transpiler Qiskit. Qiskit Fermions boleh digunakan bersama alat pelengkap lain dalam ekosistem, seperti `ffsim` (lihat [dokumentasi](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) dan [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/ffsim) ini untuk maklumat lanjut) dan [addon SQD](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), untuk membina aliran kerja lanjutan bagi sistem fermion. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See how these tools are applied in practice with the [SqDRIFT algorithm for ground state estimation](/tutorials/sqdrift) tutorial and the following guide: [Building constant-depth circuits to simulate the dynamics of the 1- and 2-D Fermi-Hubbard model](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/1-d-fermi-hubbard). Check out the [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-fermions) and [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to get started.\n"
msgstr "Lihat bagaimana alat-alat ini digunakan dalam praktik melalui tutorial [Algoritma SqDRIFT untuk anggaran keadaan asas](/tutorials/sqdrift) dan panduan berikut: [Membina litar kedalaman malar untuk mensimulasikan dinamik model Fermi-Hubbard 1-D dan 2-D](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/1-d-fermi-hubbard). Lihat [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-fermions) dan [dokumentasi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) untuk bermula.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "June 2026 {#june-2026}"
msgstr "Jun 2026 {#june-2026}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing [Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice): a new addon that integrates low-overhead quantum error detection into quantum circuits to boost the fidelity of measured distributions. It provides single-shot access to the quantum state and so can be used in both sampling-based and expectation value-based workflows. Check out the [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) and [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) for how to get started today.\n"
msgstr "Memperkenalkan [Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice): addon baharu yang mengintegrasikan pengesanan ralat kuantum dengan overhed rendah ke dalam Circuit kuantum untuk meningkatkan kesetiaan taburan yang diukur. Ia menyediakan akses single-shot kepada keadaan kuantum dan oleh itu boleh digunakan dalam aliran kerja berasaskan pensampelan mahupun berasaskan nilai jangkaan. Lihat [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) dan [dokumentasi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) untuk cara bermula hari ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Previous updates {#previous-updates}"
msgstr "Kemas kini terdahulu {#previous-updates}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We recently released two new addons that use classical resources to reduce the quantum resources needed for error mitigation:\n"
msgstr "Kami baru-baru ini melancarkan dua addon baharu yang menggunakan sumber klasik untuk mengurangkan sumber kuantum yang diperlukan bagi pengurangan ralat:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Propagated noise absorption (PNA)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-pna/) is a technique for mitigating errors in expectation values by absorbing the inverses of the learned noise channels into observables using Pauli propagation. \n"
msgstr "[Propagated noise absorption (PNA)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-pna/) ialah teknik untuk mengurangkan ralat dalam nilai jangkaan dengan menyerap songsangan saluran hingar yang telah dipelajari ke dalam observable menggunakan perambatan Pauli. \n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Shaded lightcones (SLC)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/) addon uses classical simulations to more tightly bound the sensitivity to errors throughout the circuit. This allows for more efficient, targeted applications of Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) with reduced variance.\n"
msgstr "Addon [Shaded lightcones (SLC)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/) menggunakan simulasi klasik untuk menetapkan batas yang lebih ketat bagi kepekaan terhadap ralat di seluruh Circuit. Ini membolehkan aplikasi Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) yang lebih cekap dan bersasar dengan varians yang berkurangan.\n"
